    "message": "feat(analytics): record what reasoning was requested, not just what was sent\n\nv5.33.0 gated reasoning per model, and in doing so silently changed what\nthe `reasoning` column means. `_route_for` stores the gated policy on\nRoutedMessagesRequest, and request_capture reads exactly that, so rows\nwritten before v5.33.0 record what was REQUESTED while rows written since\nrecord what was APPLIED. They agree whenever nothing was clamped and\ndiverge precisely when the interesting thing happened, with nothing\nmarking the boundary -- the same trap as the 4.25.1 and 5.13.0 steps.\n\nThis records both. `reasoning` keeps its current meaning (the applied\nvalue; every downstream consumer already treats it as what was sent, and\nflipping that twice would be worse) and `requested_reasoning` carries the\npre-gating intent. `_route_for` already computed the ungated policy before\ngating it; this stops throwing it away.\n\nNULL means \"unknown\", never \"unchanged\". Rows written before this column\nexisted genuinely have no requested value and are not backfilled or\ninferred; the documented query excludes them from the denominator rather\nthan counting them as unchanged.\n\nThe field is required on RoutedMessagesRequest with no default, so a\nfuture construction cannot silently regress the recording to\nrequested == applied. It will surface as a type error instead.\n\nMigration follows the file's existing `_ADDED_COLUMNS` + `_ensure_added_columns`\npattern: a PRAGMA table_info guard, then ALTER TABLE, with the existing\nOperationalError re-check covering a cross-process race. The column is in\n_SCHEMA too so fresh databases get it in order. It runs in _init_db rather\nthan on the writer thread because SQLite's ADD COLUMN is metadata-only --\nunlike the totals backfill and auto-vacuum conversion, which are there for\ngood reason.\n\nNo index, deliberately. `requested_reasoning <> reasoning` is a\nnon-sargable two-column expression an index on either column cannot serve;\nSQLite would scan regardless. The write path is an INSERT on every request\nwhile the query is an occasional aggregate, and a new index also perturbs\nthe planner's existing choice of idx_requests_stats_v3.\n\nFound and fixed on the way: `reasoning` appeared in the export column\norder and labels but belonged to no field entry, so the reasoning policy\nhas never been exportable at all. Both columns now hang off the `thinking`\nfield, with a standing guard that every exportable column exists in the\nschema.\n\nThe dashboard detail view shows the requested value only when it differs\nfrom the applied one; an identical second row on every request is noise.\n\nVerification:\n- 13 new tests: unchanged, clamped, suppressed and unknown-model paths;\n  migration onto a pre-existing schema; idempotency; the detail payload;\n  and an export asserting a real data cell rather than a header.\n- Migrated a 142,718-row, 800 MB copy of a live database taken with the\n  SQLite backup API: 198 ms first open, 19 ms second, zero rows lost, all\n  legacy rows NULL for the new column, existing reasoning data intact.\n- Mutation-tested: recording the applied value as the requested one failed\n  the clamped and suppressed tests by name; defeating the migration guard\n  failed 20 tests; deleting the UI difference check failed its test.\n- Full suite 4677 passed, 14 pre-existing baseline failures.\n- ruff format, ruff check, ty check clean repo-wide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
